{
  "name": "rag-your-code repository questions v1",
  "description": "Natural-language questions a developer might ask about this repository's own implementation, used to measure retrieval quality end to end. Keyed on file path and declaration name rather than line, so an edit above a declaration does not invalidate the ruler. Each question lists every unit that genuinely answers it: a single expected answer once made a correct result look like a miss.",
  "caveat": "These questions were written by the same party that wrote the code and its descriptions, so this measures 'can retrieval find the thing the author meant', not 'is the author's meaning discoverable by a stranger'. Questions are phrased the way the documentation and commit messages talk about the behaviour, not the way the descriptions do, and several are known to fail so the ruler has headroom.",
  "k": 3,
